// Example 5: Nested / composed calls (functions as values)
//
// Here calls clearly behave as values: they're arguments to other calls,
// and a function itself can be stored in a variable and called.
//
// Discussion: in square(double(3)), double(3) is an expression whose
// value is passed into square. What would change if we split it up
// into two lines? Would either line stop being an expression?

fun double(x) { return x * 2; }
fun square(x) { return x * x; }

print(square(double(3)));   // 36 - double(3) is an expression argument

var f = double;             // functions are values - f holds a function
print(f(5));                // 10 - calling through a variable
